nodecode-delegation is a rewrite of NousResearch's NousResearch/hermes-official-plugins:

  https://github.com/NousResearch/hermes-official-plugins
  commit 13b2c1c9c8204bf333df240b2aacf98c3e6250b7
  MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 Nous Research (LICENSE)

Rewritten: the plugin's `model_map` delegation backend — `model_map.py`,
plus the reading, validation and display of its settings in `store.py`
(MODES, routes, validate_route, route_summary, describe) and the
`/delegation` command of `slash.py` — as one Nodecode cell. A route is still
a name and a line the model reads over a provider, a model and an optional
reasoning effort it never sees; a task that names none still runs on the
mode's default, else on the parent's model; `/delegation` still shows the
mode with its routes and switches between them; a malformed or repeated
route is still skipped with a warning rather than guessed at. The mechanism
differs because the harness does: Hermes core owns the subagent and asks a
provider which route a task takes, while here the cell runs the subagent
itself — a fresh detached session whose model selection is the route's —
behind a `delegate` tool, and `delegation.backend` still decides whether
the model is offered the choices at all.

Left out, and why: the `profile_routes` backend and `hermes delegation
config`'s interactive editor. Profile routes exist to run a subagent as
another Hermes profile, where a profile is a config within one process; a
Nodecode profile is a separate home with its own organism, so a subagent
cannot become one in this image. The editor is replaced by the section
itself (`/settings`, the config file) and by `/delegation` for the mode;
`hermes config set delegation.backends.model_map.options` has no analogue
because the routes are the section. Also left out: Daybreak
(`daybreak: true`, OpenAI's access program), `service_tier`/`fallback_providers`/
`api_key`/`api_mode` on a route, per-route `base_url` (a Nodecode provider
section carries its endpoint), and the `delegation.model`/`delegation.provider`
keys — the parent's own model is the default, which is what those keys mean
in the mode that replaces them.
